speechtext:
Mr. ROBERT FAIR (Battle River) moved the second reading of bill No. 6, to amend the Canadian Wheat Board Act, 1935.
He said: I am very glad indeed we have an occupant in the chair; it looked for a few moments as if we were without a parliament. I am veiy glad also to find that we have an opportunity at last to discuss this measure which, to my mind, is one of great importance to all of the people of Canada.
The Canadian Wheat Board Act was passed in 1935, and the wheat board has been operating under that legislation ever since. To my mind, and I believe in the opinion of many of our farmers, both organized and unorganized, this legislation has acted to the detriment of the wheat board and the farmers of Canada as a whole. It is my intention to-night to bring about, if possible, a change in that legislation which will free the officials of the wheat board from some of the restrictions that have been imposed upon them by the original act of 1935.
Section 8, paragraphs (h), (i) and (j) read as follows:
(h)	to give effect to any order in council that may be passed with respect to its operations;
(i)	in selling and disposing of wheat as by this act provided, to utilize and employ without discrimination such marketing agencies, including commission merchants, brokers, elevator men, exporters and other persons engaged in or operating facilities for the selling and handling of wheat, as the board in its discretion may determine;
(j)	to offer wheat for sale in the markets of the world through the established channels: Provided that the board may, if in its opinion any existing agencies are not operating satisfactorily, take such steps as it deems expedient to establish, utilize and employ its own or other marketing agencies or channels.
Under these handicaps I feel that the Canadian wheat board has been compelled, perhaps against its will, to make use of the facilities which are already in operation and which I hope to show have been working to the detriment of Candian farmers and the Canadian people as a whole. In order to correct this, my amendment reads as follows. This would replace paragraphs (h), (i) and (j) which I have already read:
(h) subject to the provisions of paragraph (i) of this section, to give effect to any order in council that may be passed with respect to its operations;
Wheat Board Act
